 "said": {
  "text": "Orchestrator is the only door to the VPS; approval rules in orchestrator settings. Nothing talks to the VPS directly except the orchestrator. Claude sessions, the console, AmberX, axHub agents, headless builds — all VPS actions go through the orchestrator. The approval/veto rules live in the orchestrator's settings, and work even when no Claude session exists.",
  "verbatim": true,
  "at": "",
  "source": "console",
  "by": "headless build orchestrator-vps-gate",
  "addenda": []
 },
 "brief": "# Orchestrator is the only door to the VPS; approval rules in orchestrator settings (Brett, Nov 7)\n\nRule: nothing talks to the VPS directly except the orchestrator. Claude sessions, the console, AmberX, axHub agents, headless builds — all VPS actions go through the orchestrator. The approval/veto rules live in the **orchestrator's settings**, and work even when no Claude session exists.\n\nReuse: orchestrator-gate (orchestrator id, 0/4), build-pipeline-v2 / pipeline-v2 work (check claude/pipeline-v2 and land-ready state), vps-safe-reads (axHub branch), claude-settings-tabs-veto (its Approvals & veto tab UI can move here), axHub tool policies (allow/veto/confirm), passes.\n\n1. Contract (Fable): vps-action-policy@1 — per action kind (read, build start/stop/land, queue edit, account switch, file write, shell write, destructive) choose: run instantly | veto countdown (seconds) | needs approve; plus where alerts go (console in-place, AmberX push, both), quiet hours, per-caller overrides. Defaults: reads instant; build start/stop/land + queue edits instant; account switch + writes = veto 90 s; destructive = veto.\n2. Orchestrator settings screen (settings assets, in-place) to edit it. Approvals are shown and answered IN the console (approvals-in-place), never by jumping to axHub web.\n3. Route every VPS call through the orchestrator API (console, MCP, CLI, AmberX, headless); axHub vps tools become orchestrator-backed or restricted to the orchestrator's identity. Keep a break-glass path for Brett only.\n4. Enforce: CI check that no code outside the orchestrator calls the VPS directly.\n5. UI Review with three options (--choices). Tests for each policy mode. Add to Shipped features.\n\nProgress: append `<time> START|DONE <step>` to PROGRESS.md here at each step; don't stop between steps. Commit, don't push.",
 "models": [
  "Fable"
 ],
